<body class="mode-both">

<header>
  <h1>🌤 Why Is the Sky Blue? · 天空为什么是蓝色的？</h1>
  <p class="sub">The same question, three levels of depth, two languages · 同一个问题，三种深度，两种语言</p>
  <nav class="controls" aria-label="language view">
    <button data-mode="both" class="active">Side by side 双语对照</button>
    <button data-mode="en">English only</button>
    <button data-mode="zh">仅中文</button>
  </nav>
</header>

<main>

<!-- ============ LEVEL 1 ============ -->
<section class="level">
  <h2>🧸 Level 1 · For a 3-Year-Old · 写给 3 岁的小朋友</h2>
  <div class="pair">
    <article class="card en">
      <span class="lang-tag">English</span>
      <p>You know how sunlight looks white? It's actually made of lots of colors mixed together — like a rainbow hiding inside!</p>
      <p>When sunlight comes down to Earth, it bumps into tiny little bits in the air. The blue color is bouncy and wiggly, so it gets thrown all over the place — up, down, side to side! The other colors, like red, just go straight through.</p>
      <p>So when you look up, your eyes catch all that bouncy blue light. That's why the sky looks blue! Pretty cool, huh?</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card zh">
      <span class="lang-tag">中文</span>
      <p>你知道吗，太阳光看起来是白色的，其实它是由好多好多颜色混在一起的——就像彩虹藏在里面一样！</p>
      <p>太阳光来到地球上时，会撞进空气里那些看不见的小东西。蓝色特别调皮、特别爱蹦跶，所以被甩得到处都是——上上下下、左左右右！而其他颜色，比如红色，就直接穿过去啦。</p>
      <p>所以当你抬起头，你的眼睛就接住了那些蹦蹦跳跳的蓝光。天空就是这样变蓝的！是不是很酷呀？</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ LEVEL 2 ============ -->
<section class="level">
  <h2>🎒 Level 2 · For a High School Teenager · 写给高中生</h2>
  <div class="pair">
    <article class="card en">
      <span class="lang-tag">English</span>
      <p>Sunlight is a mix of all visible wavelengths (colors), spanning roughly 400–700 nm. When this light hits molecules in Earth's atmosphere (mostly nitrogen and oxygen), it's absorbed and re-radiated in all directions — this is <strong>scattering</strong>.</p>
      <p>The key is <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>: particles much smaller than the wavelength of light scatter shorter wavelengths <em>far</em> more strongly than longer ones. The scattering intensity goes as:</p>
      <span class="formula">I ∝ <span class="frac"><span class="num">1</span><span class="den">λ⁴</span></span></span>
      <p>So blue light (~450 nm) is scattered roughly <strong>(700/450)⁴ ≈ 5.8 times more strongly</strong> than red light (~700 nm). Blue light gets scattered into your line of sight from every direction in the sky, while reds and yellows pass through more directly.</p>
      <hr class="sep">
      <p><strong>A few extras worth knowing:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Why not violet?</strong> Violet scatters even more than blue, but the Sun emits less of it, our eyes are less sensitive to it, and the upper atmosphere absorbs some — so blue wins.</li>
        <li><strong>Why are sunsets red?</strong> At sunset, light travels a much longer path through the atmosphere. Most of the blue is scattered <em>away</em> before reaching you, leaving the reds and oranges.</li>
        <li><strong>Why does space look black?</strong> No atmosphere = no scattering. Light only travels in straight lines from its source.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="card zh">
      <span class="lang-tag">中文</span>
      <p>太阳光是所有可见光波长（颜色）的混合，大致覆盖 400–700 纳米。当光进入地球大气层，与空气中的分子（主要是氮气和氧气）碰撞时，会被吸收并向四面八方重新辐射出去——这就是<strong>散射</strong>。</p>
      <p>关键在于<strong>瑞利散射（Rayleigh scattering）</strong>：远小于光波长的微粒，对短波长光的散射能力远强于长波长光。散射强度满足：</p>
      <span class="formula">I ∝ <span class="frac"><span class="num">1</span><span class="den">λ⁴</span></span></span>
      <p>因此，蓝光（约 450 纳米）的散射强度约为红光（约 700 纳米）的 <strong>(700/450)⁴ ≈ 5.8 倍</strong>。蓝光从天空各个方向被散射进你的视线，而红光和黄光则更多地直接穿透过去。</p>
      <hr class="sep">
      <p><strong>几个值得知道的补充：</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>为什么不是紫色？</strong>紫光的散射比蓝光更强，但太阳辐射的紫光较少，人眼对紫光的敏感度较低，而且高层大气还会吸收一部分——所以最终是蓝色胜出。</li>
        <li><strong>为什么日落是红色的？</strong>日落时，光在大气中穿过的路径长得多。大部分蓝光在到达你眼睛之前就已经被散射<em>掉</em>了，只剩下红光和橙光。</li>
        <li><strong>为什么太空看起来是黑色的？</strong>没有大气 = 没有散射。光只能沿直线从光源传播而来。</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ LEVEL 3 ============ -->
<section class="level">
  <h2>🔬 Level 3 · For a Physics PhD · 写给物理学博士</h2>
  <div class="pair">
    <article class="card en">
      <span class="lang-tag">English</span>
      <p>The blue sky is a textbook consequence of <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong> by atmospheric molecules whose polarizability dominates the interaction at optical frequencies.</p>
      <p>For scatterers with size parameter <em>x</em> = 2πr/λ ≪ 1, the total scattering cross-section for an unpolarized beam is:</p>
      <span class="formula">σ<sub>s</sub> = <span class="frac"><span class="num">8π³</span><span class="den">3</span></span> · <span class="frac"><span class="num">(n² − 1)²</span><span class="den">N²λ⁴</span></span> · <span class="frac"><span class="num">6 + 3δ</span><span class="den">6 − 7δ</span></span></span>
      <p>where <em>n</em> is the refractive index, <em>N</em> the molecular number density, and <em>δ</em> ≈ 0.03 the <strong>depolarization factor</strong> accounting for the anisotropy of N₂ and O₂ (without it, you'd incorrectly predict fully polarized scattered light — observed via the sky's ~20–40% polarization, maximum at 90° scattering angle, which is how birds and insects navigate).</p>
      <hr class="sep">
      <p><strong>Some subtleties beyond the 1/λ⁴ cartoon:</strong></p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Molecular vs. aerosol regimes.</strong> Rayleigh applies for molecules (~0.3 nm). For aerosols/water droplets (λ-comparable sizes), <strong>Mie theory</strong> takes over with much weaker wavelength dependence — this is why clouds and haze appear white.</li>
        <li><strong>Density fluctuations.</strong> Einstein–Smoluchowski theory shows that Rayleigh scattering fundamentally arises from local density fluctuations (thermal fluctuations in N), not merely from the molecules as static scatterers — the same formalism explains critical opalescence near the liquid–gas critical point.</li>
        <li><strong>Multiple scattering and the spectrum.</strong> The observed sky radiance is not simply the single-scattering solar spectrum times λ⁻⁴; multiple scattering flattens the spectrum, and ozone's <strong>Chappuis absorption band</strong> (~600 nm) further suppresses reds, making the sky bluer than naive Rayleigh predicts. The zenith sky peaks near ~460 nm rather than in the violet.</li>
        <li><strong>Radiative transfer.</strong> A full treatment solves the RTE with a Rayleigh (or more precisely, Rayleigh–Gans or T-matrix for non-spherical aerosols) phase function:</li>
      </ol>
      <span class="formula">P(θ) = <span class="frac"><span class="num">3</span><span class="den">4</span></span> (1 + cos²θ)</span>
      <p>including surface albedo boundary conditions and aerosol optical depth (Ångström exponent) from measurements like AERONET.</p>
      <ol start="5">
        <li><strong>Planetary context.</strong> Titan's orange haze (tholin aerosols, Mie-dominant) and Mars's butterscotch daytime sky with bluer sunsets (fine dust scattering with strongly forward-peaked asymmetry parameter g ≈ 0.7) are useful natural experiments illustrating how sky color is a diagnostic of scatterer size distribution and composition.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Sunsets, twilight polarization patterns, and the Bishop ring in volcanic aerosol layers all fall out of the same radiative-transfer framework with modified optical properties.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card zh">
      <span class="lang-tag">中文</span>
      <p>蓝色的天空是大气分子<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的教科书式结果，在光学频段，分子的极化率（polarizability）主导了光与物质的相互作用。</p>
      <p>对于尺寸参数 <em>x</em> = 2πr/λ ≪ 1 的散射体，非偏振入射光束的总散射截面为：</p>
      <span class="formula">σ<sub>s</sub> = <span class="frac"><span class="num">8π³</span><span class="den">3</span></span> · <span class="frac"><span class="num">(n² − 1)²</span><span class="den">N²λ⁴</span></span> · <span class="frac"><span class="num">6 + 3δ</span><span class="den">6 − 7δ</span></span></span>
      <p>其中 <em>n</em> 是折射率，<em>N</em> 是分子数密度，<em>δ</em> ≈ 0.03 是<strong>退偏因子（depolarization factor）</strong>，用于修正 N₂ 和 O₂ 的各向异性（若不考虑它，就会错误地预言散射光完全偏振——实际观测到的天空偏振度约为 20%–40%，在散射角 90° 时达到最大，鸟类和昆虫正是借此导航的）。</p>
      <hr class="sep">
      <p><strong>超越 1/λ⁴ 简单图像的若干细节：</strong></p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>分子散射与气溶胶散射两个区制。</strong>瑞利散射适用于分子尺度（约 0.3 纳米）。对于与波长可比的气溶胶/水滴，<strong>米氏散射（Mie theory）</strong>占据主导，其波长依赖性弱得多——这就是云和霾呈现白色的原因。</li>
        <li><strong>密度涨落。</strong>爱因斯坦–斯莫卢霍夫斯基（Einstein–Smoluchowski）理论表明，瑞利散射从根本上源于局域密度涨落（N 的热力学涨落），而不仅仅把分子当作静态散射体——同一套形式体系也解释了液–气临界点附近的临界乳光现象。</li>
        <li><strong>多次散射与光谱。</strong>实际观测到的天空辐亮度并非简单地等于太阳光谱乘以 λ⁻⁴；多次散射会使光谱变平，而臭氧的 <strong>Chappuis 吸收带</strong>（约 600 纳米）进一步压制红光，使天空比朴素瑞利理论的预言更蓝。天顶天空的辐射峰值位于约 460 纳米，而非紫波段。</li>
        <li><strong>辐射传输。</strong>完整处理需要求解辐射传输方程（RTE），采用瑞利相函数（更精确地说，对非球形气溶胶应采用 Rayleigh–Gans 或 T 矩阵方法）：</li>
      </ol>
      <span class="formula">P(θ) = <span class="frac"><span class="num">3</span><span class="den">4</span></span> (1 + cos²θ)</span>
      <p>并纳入地表反照率边界条件，以及来自 AERONET 等观测网的气溶胶光学厚度（Ångström 指数）。</p>
      <ol start="5">
        <li><strong>行星科学的视角。</strong>土卫六（Titan）的橙色霾层（托林 tholin 气溶胶，以米氏散射为主），以及火星白天呈奶油焦糖色、日落却偏蓝的天空（细颗粒尘埃散射，强烈前冲，不对称因子 g ≈ 0.7），都是绝佳的自然实验，说明天空颜色是散射粒子尺寸分布与成分的诊断指标。</li>
      </ol>
      <p>日落、晨昏时段的偏振图样，以及火山气溶胶层中的主教环（Bishop ring），都可以在同一辐射传输框架下、通过改变光学性质参数推导出来。</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

</main>

<footer>
  sky.md · sky2.md — English &amp; 简体中文 side-by-side · no external resources
</footer>

