Now edit the slider + lens row. I need a `selectCamera` helper — declare it in the composable body (before Scaffold). Add near `updatePipelineSettings`/`saveCurrentVideoToGallery`, e.g. after `saveCurrentVideoToGallery`:

```kotlin
    val selectCamera: (String, String?) -> Unit = { id, physicalId ->
        selectedCameraId = id
        selectedPhysicalId = physicalId
        zoomValue = 1f
        livePreview.setMagnification(1f)
    }
```
Note original used `1.0f` for zoomValue and setMagnification(1.0f) — same value ✔.

Then use it in both buttons. Also extract a `LensButton(label, selected, onClick)` composable? That would dedupe the two Surface/Box/Text blocks. Both have same structure: Surface(onClick, color, shape, modifier size 40) { Box(center){Text(label, color, style)} }. Yes! Extract a private composable at file scope:

```kotlin
@Composable
private fun LensButton(
    label: String,
    selected: Boolean,
    onClick: () -> Unit
) {
    Surface(
        onClick = onClick,
        color = if (selected) MaterialTheme.colorScheme.primary else Color.Transparent,
        shape = CircleShape,
        modifier = Modifier.size(40.dp)
    ) {
        Box(contentAlignment = Alignment.Center) {
            Text(
                text = label,
                color = if (selected) Color.Black else Color.White,
                style = MaterialTheme.typography.labelMedium
            )
        }
    }
}
```
Behavior: identical composition. `Surface(onClick=...)` is the Material3 clickable Surface overload ✔.

Then:
```kotlin
                    val frontCamera = cameras.find { it.facing == CameraCharacteristics.LENS_FACING_FRONT }
                    if (frontCamera != null) {
                        LensButton(
                            label = "F",
                            selected = selectedCameraId == frontCamera.id && selectedPhysicalId == null,
                            onClick = { selectCamera(frontCamera.id, null) }
                        )
                    }

                    cameras.filter { it.isPhysical }.distinctBy { it.zoomLabel }.forEach { cam ->
                        LensButton(
                            label = cam.zoomLabel,
                            selected = selectedPhysicalId == cam.physicalId,
                            onClick = { selectCamera(cam.id, cam.physicalId) }
                        )
                    }
```
Note `isSelected` for physical compares only physicalId (original) ✔ preserved.

Careful: `cameras.filter { it.isPhysical }.distinctBy { it.zoomLabel }` — original assigned to `val physicalCameras` then forEach; same.

Slider: `valueRange = ZOOM_RANGE`, `sliderHeight = (screenMaxWidth * STILL_ASPECT_RATIO) * 0.25f` and `.height(screenMaxWidth * STILL_ASPECT_RATIO)`, remove `currentMaxWidth` alias.

